# Networking for Teacher Learning: Toward a Theory of Effective Design.

**Authors:** McDonald, Joseph P., Klein, Emily J.

## Abstract
Examines how teacher networks design for teacher learning, describing several dynamic tensions inherent in the designs of a sample of teacher networks and assessing the relationships of these tensions to teacher learning. The paper illustrates these design concepts with reference to the work of seven networks that aim to revamp teacher' knowledge in the humanities (e.g., Foxfire, Humanitas, the Bread Loaf Rural Teacher Network, and the National Writing Project). (SM)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ680010

